      "title_page_text_excerpt": "624\nMINIMUM WAGES\nMINIMUM  WAGES\nAN ORDINANCE TO AMEND THE LAW RELATING TO INDIAN LABOURERS\n[9th December, 1927.]\n1.  This Ordinance may be cited as the Minimum Wages (Indian Labour) Ordinance.\n2.   This Ordinance shall be read and construed as one with the Service Contracts Ordinance,\nthe Estate Labour (Indian) Ordinance, and the Indian Immigrant Labour Ordinance.\n3.  (1)  Where a labourer is employed at work other than time-work for a day or a successive\nnumber of days within any calendar month, the wages payable to him for that day or successive\nnumber of days, shall not be less than the wages payable to such labourer for such period at the\nminimum rates of wages prescribed under this Ordinance.\n(2)  In the case of a labourer paid by the day, any period of work performed by such person\nexceeding nine hours per day (including time not exceeding one hour taken for the midday meal) shall\nbe paid for at overtime rates, and shall be in addition to the minimum rates of wages payable to the\nlabourer for a day’s work. Such overtime rates shall not be less per hour then one-eighth of the\nminimum rates of wages prescribed under this Ordinance.\n4.  No employer shall knowingly employ for work on estates any child below the age of\nfourteen years, or knowingly permit such child to be employed.\n5.\n (1)  It shall be lawful for the Minister by notification in the Gazette to appoint for\nany administrative district an Estate Wages Board composed of five members, none of whom shall be\nmembers",
      "official_reference": "https://labourdept.gov.lk/downloads/labour_code/62.pdf",
      "reason": "The official Department of Labour copy lists Ordinances Nos. 27 of 1927 and 34 of 1935, and Act No. 25 of 2000; the original ordinance identifier is 27 of 1927."
    },
